titre$ Key to the genera Hohenbuehelia, Pleurotus e Resupinatus
com$ Adapt GF 30 nov 2018
1,0$source : "The Genera Hohenbuehelia and Resupinatus in Europe" ///Giovanni Consiglio(Author), Ledo Setti(Author)/// 2017 Monografie di Pagine di Micologia Volume: 3
1,0$
1,2 $ Fungi nematophagous
1,3 $ Fungi non-nematophagous
2,0 $ Pileus covering with a gelatinous layer. Two types of cystidia: a) metuloid cystidia covered with calcium oxalate crystals, metachromatic in cresyl blue, present on the lamellae and sometimes in pileipellis and b) cystidia thin-walled, davate or fusiform with one or more finger-like swellings and tipped with an hourglass-shaped structure, surrounded by an evanescent drop of mucus, present on the edge and on the face of the lamellae and sometimes in pileipellis (gloeosphexes). Pileus covering a cutis, an ixocutis, a trichoderm, or an ixotrichoderm with tufts of more or less perpendicular hyphae agglutinated by the gel. Species of Hohenbuehelia!Nematoctonus capture nematodes by the production of adhesive knobs, which surround hour-glass-shaped secretory appendages$Genus Hohenbuehelia
2,0 $ Pileus covering without a gelatinous layer. Metuloid cystidia absent but often davate, rostrate to lecythiform cystidium-like basidioles present. Pileipellis a cutis. Species oiPleurotus capture nematodes by production of liquid microdroplets containing a nematotoxin on secretory appendages on fine, tapering pegs that are scattered on aerial somatic hyphae $ Genus Pleurotus
3,0 $ Pileus covering with a gelatinous layer. Metuloid hymenial cystidia absent (except ini?, niger). Cheilocystidia coralloid, branched, dendrophysoid, often covered with crystals, thin walled. Pileipellis often with a Ramealis type structure, consisting of coralloid-diverticulate hyphae that secrete hyaline or brownish crystalline material by thin cylindrical or tapered tips $ Genus Resupinatus
